  "description": "Decodes image files and streams (PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP and WebP experimental; GIF with transparency rejected) with SkiaSharp into Starlings.Models.EmbeddingGemma2 images, reproducing PIL's convert(\"RGB\") as the upstream processor sees it: alpha dropped (not composited), grayscale and palettes expanded, CMYK converted, no colour management, EXIF orientation ignored unless explicitly applied (a documented deviation from upstream). Images with 16 bits per channel are rejected (upstream saturates them to white). Decoded size limit 50 megapixels by default. Brings SkiaSharp (MIT) and its Linux natives (SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.Linux.NoDependencies), whose bundled third-party notices include an MPL-1.1 GIF decoder and the Adobe DNG SDK license. Maturity is per model profile (Stable, Preview or Experimental): see the README, generated from the model registry.",
